// A host that holds a NUL byte is a runtime error for connect
// (spec/05-stdlib.md, Strings the host reads): getaddrinfo() reads the name
// only up to the NUL, so the call would connect to a different host. The
// fault is not catchable, so a consumer that raises the catchable NetworkError
// of a failed connection instead prints its kind and goes on.
// STATUS: error
// CHECK: before
// COVERS: host-string connect
print "before";
try { connect("127.0.0.1" + chr(0) + "tail", 1); } catch (e) { print "caught " + e.kind; }
print "not caught";
